From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:39:18 -0600
Subject: Web: expose the Wasm worker's script URL

A Web Assembly worker runs from a blob URL that holds Squadron's loader
script (EntryPointUri._wasmLoaderScript in
lib/src/_impl/web/_entry_point_uri.dart), so inside the worker
self.location is the blob, not the worker's files. Code in the worker
that loads sibling assets (a wasm-bindgen module next to the worker,
for instance) has no reliable base URL and ends up guessing from the
origin, which is wrong whenever the app is not served from the origin
root.

The loader already derives the absolute URL of the worker's .wasm file
(workerUri). Assign it to globalThis.squadronWorkerScriptUrl right
after deriving it, before the Dart runtime is imported or main is
invoked, so the worker can resolve relative paths against its real
location. self.location, the blob, the worker packaging and the channel
protocol are unchanged. JavaScript workers do not need it: they run
from their own URL. The loader is the only place that knows the
worker's real URL, and the global is inert for code that ignores it.
It is deliberately not namespaced (a worker has no module system); the
name follows the loader's workerUri.

Tests: test/web_worker_script_url_test.dart (browser only) fetches the
blob's loader script of a Wasm entry point and checks that
`globalThis.squadronWorkerScriptUrl=workerUri;` comes after
`const workerUri=` and before `let newRt=`, and that a .js entry point
keeps its own URL. It does not observe the value inside a running
worker; that needs a Wasm test worker reporting it, i.e. a new service
method and rebuilt worker binaries.

Checks run on fd5becc (7.4.5) with this as the only commit (fork branch
web-worker-script-url @ 915a6517, where the CHANGELOG entry has its own
"Unreleased" section), Dart 3.13.7, Chrome 157.0.8103.50:
- `dart analyze` reports no issues.
- `dart test -p vm`: 689 passed, 5 skipped.
- After `dart run tool/compile_tests.dart js wasm` (as in
  tool/run_tests.sh), `dart test -p chrome --compiler dart2js`: 1462
  passed, 10 skipped, including the JS and the WASM runner suites, so
  real Wasm workers still load through the changed loader.
- The new test passes with the change and fails at fd5becc ("wasm
  worker loader exposes the worker script url"), so it is a regression
  test.

Rebase notes: in this series the CHANGELOG entry shares the
"Unreleased" section with the channel factory entry; the test file was
taken from the fork branch, which the previously carried patch lacked.

